{
  "verdict": "Policy adoption yields between runs. The calibrated 6000-run, 750 ms regression passed 10/10 on fixed code and failed 10/10 on old code. Earlier mixed-workload results remain shared-host observations; other synchronous stages and the historical production stall remain open.",
  "base": "4fbd30cb",
  "bun": "1.4.3",
  "platform": "macOS arm64",
  "cores": 10,
  "dataset": {
    "benchmarkCases": 10000,
    "versions": 15932,
    "automatedTests": 4000,
    "results": 105123,
    "openQuestions": 5000,
    "demoCases": 500,
    "demoDays": 2
  },
  "method": "Five alternating before/after pairs, fresh disk copy and process per run, production NODE_ENV, production WAL/checkpoint pragmas, eight ready reader workers. Independent process probes health every 125 ms after the previous response; server logs setInterval(20 ms) drift above 10 ms. Report has 4000 results, 200 earlier tries, 20 attachments. Columns are the median and full range of each run's longest health wait, not request percentiles. No throughput claim.",
  "limitations": [
    "The shared host ran browser tests, other checks, Xcode and indexing. Load reached about 100 on 10 cores. Absolute waits include OS scheduling and storage contention. Profilers were not enabled on any reported server; a separate diagnostic server overlapped pair three and added host load.",
    "Original pair five after-side failed its untimed 5-second reader readiness check. Both sides were rerun with a 60-second untimed readiness allowance. The failed run and original extra before-side are excluded; all five successful pairs are retained.",
    "The after-side third window exceeded 60 seconds, so the instance minute timer may also have run. Events below identify concurrent workload, not unique causal attribution. The manual renewDemoWork call is labelled separately.",
    "Cold process/schema paths and warm reader readiness are identical on both sides. Local mode authorizes benchmark administrative requests; reports use a scoped CI token. This is a source Bun server, not a compiled container or production network.",
    "The historical instance 17-second stall remains unattributed. The selected latency regression passed its author campaign, but independent verification, full-check and timing refresh remain with the coordinator."
  ],
  "correctness": "All reported health requests succeeded. Each of the ten CI reports returned fresh=true, counts.total=4000; gate, change, archive, find and Queue calls succeeded and returned populated output. Every policy adoption returned decided with policyVersion=2, ruled=101; a subsequent admin read required version=2 and preset=loose. A separate smoke run of the checked-in harness additionally checks 4000 stored results, 200 stored tries, 20 attachments and an extended demo lease.",
  "profile": {
    "reported": false,
    "beforeDiagnosticPolicyStepMs": 3312.567458,
    "beforeDiagnosticPolicyHealthMaxMs": 3188.1,
    "source": "reconsiderPolicySteps -> refold -> per-run inheritance, retally, askUnexplained and dissolveStale; candidate rule questions then settle synchronously",
    "cpuSampleInclusiveMs": {
      "reconsiderPolicySteps": 3310,
      "refold": 2349,
      "askUnexplained": 1175
    },
    "afterDiagnostic": "reconciliation is split into yielded generator steps; longest measured decide next() was 629 ms on the overloaded host, so per-run work and scheduling pauses remain. Diagnostic samples are excluded from the table."
  },
